  "notes": "The Andersons, Inc. (NASDAQ: ANDE). Diversified North American agribusiness \u2014 three reportable segments: Trade (grain origination/merchandising/storage; ~7M tons capacity Eastern Corn Belt + acquired Skyland 2024), Renewables (4 ethanol plants ~480MGY plus DDG byproducts; consolidated post-2021 buyout of LP partners), and Plant Nutrient (specialty fertilizers / lawn / homeowner). Fiscal year ends Dec 31. Data from SEC EDGAR XBRL companyfacts (CIK 0000821026). Note: ANDE does NOT report a US-GAAP `OperatingIncomeLoss` line in its consolidated statements \u2014 this segment of the income statement is gross-profit-driven (revenue \u2212 cost of sales/merchandising). EBITDA computed as net income before tax + interest + D&A using directly-tagged D&A. Shares from cover page (`EntityCommonStockSharesOutstanding`). Revenue swung wildly with grain price cycle: FY22 record $17.3B (Russia/Ukraine spike); FY23 $14.8B; FY24 $11.3B (post-glut deflation). Skyland Grain acquired Apr 2024 (180M).",
